1 BUILD3~
BUILDING GUIDE - MOBILE COMBAT BASICS
=====================================

MCREATE <vnum> [copy-vnum] <keywords>
MLIST [low high]
MFIND <name>
MINVOKE <vnum>
MSET <mob> <field> <value>
SAVEAREA

D20-READY MOBILE BALANCE
-------------------------
LEVEL
  Existing mobile level feeds the broad 0-100 advancement system. Combat BAB
  is translated at roughly one heroic step per five levels.

ATTRIBUTES
  Use believable ability scores. Ordinary Humans cluster around 8-14; trained
  specialists commonly reach 14-18. Values far above 20 should be exceptional.

ARMOR / DEFENSE
  The legacy AC field is translated to ascending Defense. Avoid extreme negative
  legacy AC such as -100 or -300. A legacy armor value of 100 is +0 armor
  Defense, 90 is +1, 80 is +2, 70 is +3, and so on.

HITROLL / DAMROLL
  These are direct modifiers on top of BAB and ability modifiers. Ordinary mobs
  should usually use 0 to +2. Large old-style +10/+20 values are no longer
  appropriate.

DAMAGE
  Use d20-scale weapon/natural damage. A low-level humanoid might deal around
  1d4 to 1d8 before ability bonuses; stronger weapons and creatures can scale
  upward deliberately.

SAVES
  New encounter design should think in Fortitude, Reflex and Will against DCs.

See also: ABILITYMODIFIER BAB DEFENSE SAVINGTHROWS DIFFICULTYCLASS BUILD4
~

1 BUILD4~
Local Sphere Building Pg 4
                       OBJECT BUILDING BASICS
***************************************************************************

OCREATE <vnum> [cvnum] <namelist>  Creates a new object.                        

OLIST                              Lists objects in your area.
OLIST <from> <to>                  Lists objects within the given range.

OFIND <name>                       Lists all objects with that name.

OINVOKE <vnum>                     Creates a new instance of the object.

OSET <object> <field> <value>      Try typing oset by itself to get a list
                                   of fields. Then "oset <object> <field>
                                   to get a list of values for that field.
                                   You should set the type first.

SAVEAREA                           Do this alot                      

***************************************************************************
~

0 BUY LIST SELL VALUE~
Syntax: buy   <object>
Syntax: buy   <# of object> <object>
Syntax: list
Syntax: list  <object>
Syntax: sell  <object>
Syntax: value <object>

BUY buys an object from a shop keeper.
BUY <# of object> <object> will allow you to buy up to twenty of a normal
store item at once.

LIST lists the objects the shop keeper will sell you.  LIST <object> lists
just the objects with that name.

SELL sells an object to a shop keeper.

VALUE asks the shop keeper how much he, she, or it will buy the item for.
~

