1 SPACE SHIP SHIPS PILOTING FLIGHT SPACECRAFT~
Common spacecraft commands include:

  SHIPS                    list ships available for sale or rent
  BOARD <ship>             enter a ship
  LEAVESHIP                leave a ship
  LAUNCH                   launch from the current dock
  LAND <location>          land at a valid dock
  SPEED <value>            change speed
  COURSE <x y z>           steer toward a vector
  STATUS                   display ship status
  INFO <ship>              inspect a ship
  RADAR                    scan the local system
  CALCULATE <system>       prepare a long-range FTL route
  HYPERSPACE               execute the prepared FTL transition
  BUYSHIP / SELLSHIP       buy or sell a ship
  SHIELDS                  control defensive shields
  RECHARGE                 accelerate shield recharge
  OPENHATCH / CLOSEHATCH   control access
  TARGET <ship>            select a target
  FIRE                     fire the selected weapon system
  REPAIRSHIP               repair hull or ship systems
  ADDPILOT / REMPILOT      manage authorized pilots
  AUTOTRACK                automatically follow a selected target
  CLANBUYSHIP              purchase a ship for an organization

Piloting checks should use Dexterity; navigation, systems and technical repair
generally use Intelligence. Where a task can fail, it should resolve through
the standard skill-check and Difficulty Class rules.

See also: PILOTING NAVIGATION SKILLCHECK
~

