The WHOIS command will tell you a bit of information about a player
who is online.
 
See BIO
~

0 WIMPY~
Syntax: wimpy
Syntax: wimpy <number>

WIMPY sets your wimpy value.  When your character takes damage that reduces
your hit points below your wimpy value, you will automatically attempt to flee.

WIMPY with no argument sets your wimpy value to 20% of your maximum hit points.

Some monsters are wimpy.
~

1 WISDOM WIS~
Wisdom (WIS) measures perception, judgement, intuition and self-control.

Its ability modifier is:

  modifier = floor((WIS - 10) / 2)

Wisdom contributes to Will saving throws and commonly governs perception,
tracking, first aid and other judgement-based skills.

See also: ABILITYMODIFIER WILL SKILLCHECK FIRSTAID TRACK
~

101 WIZHELP~
Syntax: wizhelp

WIZHELP provides a list of all the immortal commands.
~

0 WIZLIST~
Syntax: wizlist

Displays a hierarchical list of immortals.
~

0 Vordan Vordans~
Vordans are large, physically powerful sophonts adapted to demanding
environments. Their culture values endurance, reliability and direct action,
but Vordan engineers and technicians are as important to their society as
their soldiers.

Ability modifiers:
  STR +4  DEX -2  CON +2  INT +0  WIS -2  CHA -2

Homeworld: GJ 273 b
Typical strengths: melee combat, carrying capacity, physical endurance.
~

