0 TRAIT TRAITS TRAITLIST~
Syntax: TRAITS
Syntax: TRAITS LIST

Every character has six personal traits: four positive traits and two
negative traits. Traits are generated with the character and become permanent
when the character is accepted.

Traits have three ranks:

  Rank I    modifier 1
  Rank II   modifier 2
  Rank III  modifier 4

Positive and negative trait packages are balanced. Trait effects may modify
ability potential, saving throws, weapon aptitude, piloting, technical skills,
social skills, crafting or other specific systems.

For core abilities, trait potential contributes to the natural training cap:

  Natural Potential = 20 + racial modifier + trait potential modifier

See also: TRAIN NATURALPOTENTIAL SAVINGTHROWS SKILLS
~

0 ABILITYMODIFIER ABILITYMOD ABILITYMODIFIERS~
An ability modifier converts a core ability score into the bonus or penalty
used by checks.

  modifier = floor((score - 10) / 2)

Examples:
   3 = -4      8 = -1     10 = +0     12 = +1
  14 = +2     16 = +3     18 = +4     20 = +5

STR, DEX, CON, INT, WIS and CHA use this formula.

See also: STRENGTH DEXTERITY CONSTITUTION INTELLIGENCE WISDOM CHARISMA
~

0 BAB BASEATTACKBONUS "BASE ATTACK BONUS"~
Base Attack Bonus (BAB) represents general combat competence.

The current conversion derives BAB from Combat Ability. Each five points of
Combat Ability correspond to one heroic step, producing BAB from +1 through
+20.

BAB is part of both melee and ranged attack rolls.

See also: ATTACKROLL COMBAT LEVEL
~

0 ATTACKROLL ATTACKROLLS "ATTACK ROLL"~
Attack rolls use a twenty-sided die against ascending Defense.

Melee:
  d20 + BAB + STR modifier + proficiency + traits + other modifiers

Ranged:
  d20 + BAB + DEX modifier + proficiency + traits + other modifiers

A total equal to or greater than the target's Defense hits.
Natural 1 misses. Natural 20 hits.

See also: BAB DEFENSE COMBAT
~

0 DEFENSE DEFENCE~
Defense is the target number for ordinary attacks. Higher is better.

Current compatibility formula:

  Defense = 10 + heroic Defense bonus + DEX modifier + armor bonus

The armor bonus is translated from the existing area/object armor field while
legacy content is converted.

Sleeping or otherwise unable-to-react targets may lose Dexterity-based
protection.

See also: ARMOR DEXTERITY ATTACKROLL
~

0 SKILLCHECK SKILLCHECKS "SKILL CHECK"~
A skill check resolves a task against a Difficulty Class (DC):

  d20 + skill bonus + governing ability modifier + trait + modifiers >= DC

Typical governing abilities:
  DEX - piloting, stealth, lock work
  INT - engineering, slicing, navigation, crafting, investigation
  WIS - first aid, tracking, perception
  CHA - diplomacy, leadership and social influence
  STR - direct physical techniques where appropriate

A natural 1 or 20 is not automatically a failure or success on an ordinary
skill check unless the specific skill says otherwise.

See also: DIFFICULTYCLASS SKILLS PRACTICE
~

0 DIFFICULTYCLASS DC "DIFFICULTY CLASS"~
Difficulty Class (DC) is the target number for skill checks and many saving
throws.

General guidance:
  DC  5  trivial
  DC 10  easy
  DC 15  standard
  DC 20  difficult
  DC 25  very difficult
  DC 30  heroic
  DC 35+ exceptional

Use a DC appropriate to the task rather than converting every old percentage
check literally.

See also: SKILLCHECK SAVINGTHROWS
~

0 NATURALPOTENTIAL "NATURAL POTENTIAL"~
Natural Potential is the highest permanent core ability score a character can
reach through ordinary training.

  Natural Potential = 20 + racial modifier + trait potential modifier

Permanent training cannot exceed that personal cap. Cybernetics, equipment and
temporary effects may raise the effective score above it.

See also: TRAIN TRAITS RACES
~

0 PSIONICS PSIONIC~
Psionics is the Local Sphere term for rare trained mental disciplines.

Psionic Potential determines whether a character can develop these abilities.
Individual disciplines still use the ordinary rules framework: attacks,
saving throws, skills and Difficulty Classes.

Psionics is not a substitute for the six core abilities.

See also: POTENTIAL FRC FEEL MEDITATE
~

0 EARTH SOL "SOL SYSTEM"~
Earth is the Human homeworld and the political centre of the Sol system. In the
Local Sphere setting, The Hague is a major interstellar diplomatic and civic
hub.

Species: Human
System: Sol
Key location: The Hague
~

0 GJ273B "GJ 273 B" "GJ 273"~
GJ 273 b is the Vordan homeworld in the GJ 273 system. In the game setting its
settlements are built around durable industrial infrastructure and communities
adapted to demanding local conditions.

Species: Vordan
~

0 TEEGARDEN "TEEGARDEN'S STAR B"~
Teegarden's Star b is the Lethari homeworld. In the game setting it is a major
centre of commerce, diplomacy and interstellar exchange.

Species: Lethari
System: Teegarden's Star
~

0 ROSS128B "ROSS 128 B" "ROSS 128"~
Ross 128 b is the Keshari homeworld. In the game setting its culture and
settlements emphasize exploration, fieldcraft and environmental observation.

Species: Keshari
~

0 LHS1140B "LHS 1140 B" "LHS 1140"~
LHS 1140 b is the Pelagian homeworld. In the game setting Pelagian civilization
is strongly associated with aquatic habitats, navigation and pressure
engineering.

Species: Pelagian
~

0 PROXIMAB "PROXIMA CENTAURI B"~
Proxima Centauri b is the Drakken homeworld. In the game setting its settlements
use hardened infrastructure and careful environmental protection.

Species: Drakken
System: Proxima Centauri
~

0 TRAPPIST1E "TRAPPIST-1 E"~
TRAPPIST-1 e is the Veyran homeworld and a major technical centre in the
TRAPPIST-1 system.

Species: Veyran
~

0 TRAPPIST1F "TRAPPIST-1 F"~
TRAPPIST-1 f is the Noxian homeworld. In the game setting its settlements and
orbital facilities are optimized for low-light living and careful resource use.

Species: Noxian
~

0 BARNARDB "BARNARD B" "BARNARD'S STAR"~
Barnard b is an important independent frontier world in the Local Sphere.
Barnard Freeport and its orbital facilities support trade, transport and
frontier activity.

System: Barnard's Star
~

0 COREMECHANICS RULESYSTEM~
The Local Sphere rules use a unified twenty-sided resolution framework.

ABILITY MODIFIER
  floor((score - 10) / 2)

ATTACKS
  d20 + BAB + ability modifier + proficiency + modifiers vs Defense

SAVES
  Fortitude uses CON
  Reflex uses DEX
  Will uses WIS

SKILLS
  d20 + skill bonus + governing ability modifier + traits + modifiers vs DC

TRAINING
  Permanent abilities cannot naturally exceed personal Natural Potential.

See also: ABILITYMODIFIER ATTACKROLL DEFENSE SAVINGTHROWS SKILLCHECK
NATURALPOTENTIAL
~

